normalpowers
============

normalpowers is a derivative work of superpowers
(https://github.com/obra/superpowers) by Jesse Vincent, licensed under MIT.

We are deeply grateful to Jesse and everyone who contributed to superpowers.
The interview-style thinking skills — brainstorming, writing-plans,
systematic problem-solving, verification-before-completion, receiving
feedback, and writing-skills — originated in superpowers and carry its DNA.

What differs:

  - superpowers is a Claude Code / Cursor / Codex / OpenCode / Gemini CLI
    plugin tuned for software engineering.
  - normalpowers is a portable markdown prompt bundle tuned for generalist
    knowledge workers. It drops all plugin machinery, hooks, subagent
    dispatch, git-worktree and test-suite assumptions, and works on any LLM
    that accepts a system prompt (Claude.ai, ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude API,
    etc.).

Software-specific skills were removed in the fork's initial cleanup; the
remaining skills were rewritten with knowledge-work examples in place of
code examples. See docs/comparison-to-superpowers.md for the full diff in
intent.

Upstream remains the source of truth for new philosophy; we track it at
https://github.com/obra/superpowers and cherry-pick selectively. See
docs/upstream-sync.md for the process.
